#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:102
msgid "How coexistence works"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:103
msgid "Left alone, whichever of the two hooks netfilter first wins and the other does nothing. Coexistence moves the dividing line onto UU's side: only what UU actually accelerates leaves the proxy, and only for devices it is boosting. Everything else from that same device keeps going through the proxy - so most of a boosted PC's traffic still showing up there is the intended result, not a fault.<br /><br /><strong>Split the traffic</strong> - the split described above. The recommended one.<br /><strong>Take whole devices off the proxy</strong> - the blunt fallback: a boosted device skips the proxy entirely, whatever it is talking to. For the device that will not split cleanly.<br /><strong>Leave it alone</strong> - the two are left to fight over the packets."
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:121
msgid "Redirects LAN traffic from chains inside fw4. The exemption is UU's own destination routes, plus the UDP ports and fwmark UU sets - all read back from its live rules, because they differ between builds."
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:125
msgid "Drives mihomo behind an nftables table of its own. DNS is exempted too, because UU sends a boosted device's lookups through its tunnel. Give it a <code>redir-host</code> DNS profile: fake-ip breaks the boost."
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:129
msgid "Only its TUN mode with auto-redirect is handled. In its other modes the traffic is hooked inside fw4, out of reach - add the device under HomeProxy's own Access Control instead."
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:133
msgid "Rewrites the User-Agent of LAN traffic by diverting TCP to itself. Only TCP is exempted, because that is all UA3F touches."
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:144
msgid "Split the traffic (recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:149
msgid "Take whole devices off the proxy"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:151
msgid "Leave it alone"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:159
msgid "No proxy installed"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:160
msgid "There is nothing to coexist with: no OpenClash, Nikki, HomeProxy or UA3F was found on this router. Install one and its setting appears here."
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:171
msgid "OpenClash: move boosted devices off its bypass list"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:172
msgid "OpenClash keeps a list of devices that skip the proxy completely (lan_ac_black_ips), and a device on it returns before any finer exemption can apply. Turn this on to take such a device off that list while it is boosted and put it back afterwards. Off by default, because it edits and saves OpenClash's config."
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:184
msgid "Re-check interval"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:185
msgid "Seconds between re-reads of UU's route list. UU adds and removes game routes while it runs, and every proxy above follows this interval."
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:191
msgid "Widest route to divert"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:192
msgid "A safety limit, as a prefix length: a route broader than this is never sent around the proxy. Stops one stray default route from pulling the whole internet out of it."
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:201
msgid "Devices UU is allowed to see"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:202
msgid "Every device on the network"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:203
msgid "Everything except the devices below"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:204
msgid "Only the devices below"
msgstr ""

#: luci-app-uugamebooster/luasrc/model/cbi/uuplugin.lua:206
msgid "The UU app lists whatever the plugin finds on your network, which by default is everything. This narrows what it can find at all, so a device left out never appears in the app, is never offered for boosting, and is never reported to NetEase.<br />Nothing else on the router is affected: the real DHCP leases and ARP table are untouched, and no traffic is blocked."
msgstr ""

